      "writtenOn": "2025-05-20T01:13:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it is basically _the_ segment register value (i.e. after a vmexit we can read the current value of this segment register from this VMCS field). And yeah, it seems it doesn\u0027t matter what we write to it: before the guest reloads the segment register, the cached descriptor set up below is used instead, and once the guest reloads it, the new value loaded by the guest is used instead.\n\nAs by the assumption there is no valid GDT (per the comment about GDT below), there can be no valid value of the selector either, so it makes sense to set it to 0?",
